# The comparison corpus that the "nothing a release found is lost" claims of 0.10.0 and 0.11.0
# cite. The corpus is not in this repository (7,715 patches, 72 planted Git repositories, the
# frozen release binaries); it is named here by the SHA-256 of its manifest, the last line of
# this file. The local gate's step "comparison corpus manifest" verifies the corpus where it
# exists.
#
# 0.11.0. Added to the corpus on 2026-11-24, which is why its digest moved from the 0.10.0 one
# (a6e6baff0360a41860ce9c1d24a7bdc3a58b0989c2cd3f6c8f1e57adb0674ec2, the record further down):
# four sibling batteries for the readings this release widened (assert-class, let-drop,
# panic-macro, cfg-test: 294 patches), nine planted Git rows for a source file that a stray byte
# makes binary by content (27 repositories; the 45 earlier ones rebuild unchanged), the
# published 0.10.0 binary and the binaries below.
#
# The release-prepared commit 2843998a (version 0.11.0; binary sha256
# 32fe5aa132aafd11cac94a4873ad884d5bd28038b49291db834591857f7f12dc, a release-profile Cargo build
# of that commit, not the release build), run 2026-11-24T15:47Z, record
# runs/20261124T154702Z-32fe5aa132aa of the corpus: every figure and every result file of the
# record below, and with the version string written as 0.11.0 the same stdout, stderr and exit
# code as the reviewed binary c19cf99c… on all 7,715 patches in --json, --rank --json and
# --diagnostics --json. No Rust source file changes between the two commits; the version does.
#
# Whole-tree record for the candidate after the tree review's fix round, commit b8532c32 (version
# 0.11.0-dev; binary sha256 c19cf99c6c2e3509be4d4dc1050cd2b8c65c459faef56a609c9d8ce25d9ea208, the
# release-profile Cargo build of that commit), run 2026-11-24T13:34Z, record
# runs/20261124T133439Z-c19cf99c6c2e of the corpus:
#   identity control                               lost 0    gained 0
#   against the published 0.10.0 (121503a8…)       lost 106  gained 1002  (see note 3)
#   against v0.9.0 code (5ba0a366…)                lost 160  gained 1244  (note 3: 106; note 2: 54)
#   against v0.8.4 (0c93b3ed…)                     lost 101  gained 2394  (note 3: 100; note 1: 1)
#   against v0.8.3 (4cafd0ad…)                     lost 101  gained 2432  (note 3: 100; note 1: 1)
#   Refusals against the published 0.10.0: 1,410 patches refused by both, none differs.
#   Git selections against the published 0.10.0, 72 planted repositories and 8 history ranges:
#   no planted repository loses an item in any mode, and 7 in each mode gain one (the stray-byte
#   rows: diff_suppressed, and the code label where there is one, where 0.10.0 gave binary_change
#   alone). In 2 of the 8 history ranges items are lost: 49 check_suppressed, each of note 3, and
#   30 panic_path_added in four files whose evidence list is cut at its 32 rows in both builds:
#   this build lists items it gained on earlier lines, every lost row lies after its last listed
#   row, and each file keeps the label.
# Note 3, a listed exception to the floor (0.11.0, the contract register's row F2b.g): `#[allow(`
#   inside a Rust comment or a string is no check_suppressed, and `r#unsafe`, an identifier, is
#   no unsafe_added. All 106 patches lost against 0.10.0 are that and nothing else, read from the
#   item differences with nothing cut (the corpus's tools/diffitems.py and tools/lostclass.py):
#   251 items in lists neither build cut, on 95 patches (197 in a string, 50 in a line comment, 1
#   in a block comment, 3 `r#unsafe`), each read at its line; 14 files in 11 patches that lose
#   the label on a list 0.10.0 had cut at its 32 rows, where every added line naming `allow(` is
#   a comment or a string; and 172 rows that are in one build's cut list and not the other's, in
#   files that keep the label (the bound). Counted over every list, cut or not, it is the 478
#   rows and 116 files the changelog gives. This note first said "191 listed items": that was
#   the count of a log that prints five items a file (corrected 2026-11-25 after the tree
#   review, finding A0110-L2).
# The same record was taken before on 5030ae9b (binary 704f66e9…, record
#   runs/20261124T103801Z-704f66e94b68), on b337eb2c (b329a52b…, runs/20261124T105927Z-b329a52b8f89)
#   and on 4ad1ca73 (6e49cb19…, runs/20261124T113029Z-6e49cb194eab, the commit the reviewers
#   read), which differ from this commit in texts of the hooks and in what `agent verify-branch`
#   refuses: every result file is the same in the four but for the binary's name, and the four
#   binaries give the same stdout, stderr and exit code on all 7,715 patches in --json,
#   --rank --json and --diagnostics --json.
#
# 0.10.0 (corpus digest a6e6baff0360a41860ce9c1d24a7bdc3a58b0989c2cd3f6c8f1e57adb0674ec2: 7,421
# patches, 45 planted Git repositories).
# Whole-tree record for the release-prepared commit 2343eef1 (version 0.10.0; binary sha256
# df8359c42d99a957c5266825b1d8e87c84b7b7d6aaeb30753527454b321c3e6f, the release-profile Cargo
# build of that commit; the published 0.10.0 binary, its reproducible build, is
# 121503a8d292da951c31e33e8b59bf33b54dd316e3d6ec3055e5c4bfac18e9ff: named 2026-11-23, EVIDENCE.md
# "0.10.0 binaries and commits by name"; "v0.9.0 code (5ba0a366…)" below is a build of the
# 0.9.0 code, the published 0.9.0 binary being 83158afe…), run 2026-11-23T02:31Z,
# record runs/20261123T023136Z-df8359c42d99 of the corpus:
#   identity control                 lost 0   gained 0
#   against v0.8.3 (4cafd0ad…)       lost 1   gained 2063   (see note 1)
#   against v0.8.4 (0c93b3ed…)       lost 1   gained 2025   (see note 1)
#   against v0.9.0 code (5ba0a366…)  lost 54  gained 242    (see note 2)
#   against the binary both reviewers first read (7ffb5c33…, commit 1b1d4a49): lost 0, gained 0,
#   and with the tool's version member normalised the same stdout, stderr and exit code on
#   every patch.
#   Git selections, 45 planted repositories and 8 history ranges, against v0.9.0 code and against
#   the first fix of this release: every lost item is binary_change on a file that gains
#   diff_suppressed; no file lost a label without gaining one.
# Note 1: one patch holds two sections for one path; both releases and this tree report new_file
#   on it. Since 0.9.0 the two entries come out in the other order (the entry with process_spawn
#   ranks first), so the comparison, which keys an entry by path and position, pairs them
#   differently. No label is missing.
# Note 2: all 54 are trivial_assert on Python lines where "assert True" is followed by more
#   (for example "assert True == False"), which 0.9.0 labelled though they can fail: the narrowing
#   of task S3.16, a recorded exception to the floor.
bddd0a41ffc48a67fd798f6805e36da4324fb30adde0a903e363436962004dc6  MANIFEST.sha256
